Security integration contract
-----------------------------
Run node patches/dsh/patch-host.mjs RUNTIME_DIRECTORY exactly once after
installation, before starting DSH. Unknown versions, altered inputs and
already-patched files are rejected. All discovered pnpm package copies are
validated before writes. Preserve patched packages on the immutable rootfs.
The patched WebServer always requires an access gate from first accept.
registerRequiredAccessGate({http,upgrade}) is synchronous and exclusive;
requiredAccessGateVersion is required-access-gate-v1. Missing gate: HTTP 503.
Gate exceptions clear registration and close accepted sockets; disposal clears
registration and closes HTTP streams, keepalive and upgraded sockets. No
private server listener takeover, relay, custom parser, or unguarded fallback.

Activate the bundle @soulwhisper/dsh-forward-auth in every served profile; the
patch inserts required Host-only distribution-forward-auth with
webServer+connection injection. The app-boot exact patch adds
distribution-forward-auth to requiredStartupEntryIds, the native required-entry
policy (Loader has no required:true row property).

DSH_FORWARD_AUTH_HEADER is mandatory and names exactly one request header that
the trusted edge injects. Authentik commonly uses x-authentik-uid; Authelia can
use Remote-User. The header is configurable; no provider-specific path is
assumed. DSH_FORWARD_AUTH_ALLOWED_SUBJECTS is a mandatory comma-separated stable
subject allowlist. DSH_FORWARD_AUTH_TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS is a mandatory
comma-separated concrete IP CIDR set; no forwarded address header is trusted.
Mapped IPv6 peers match IPv4 CIDRs; write mapped networks as native IPv4 CIDRs.
Duplicate or malformed identity, Host, Origin and Cookie headers fail closed.
Host and Origin are never rewritten.

DSH_FORWARD_AUTH_MAX_CONNECTION_SECONDS defaults to 900 and bounds every
admitted upgrade; its positive integer value must fit a Node timer. Admission
always requires external identity, even with valid native browser/API cookies.
This is a shared-owner harness, not a multiuser authorization boundary. There is
no local password, bootstrap admin, OIDC client or user database.

The upstream DSH launch-token URL is not an authentication bypass. The gate
rejects any request whose query contains a `token` parameter, including
WebSocket upgrades, before the native Connection is consulted. The native
connection's internal clean-root cookie exchange remains the only supported
bootstrap path after the edge has supplied an allowlisted identity. Startup
stdout may still contain the upstream launch URL; treat logs as sensitive and
do not publish them.

The native Connection requestRejection fence executes before cookie exchange.
Native 403 stays 403. On 401 only, authenticatedUrl and authorizeIndex exchange
a native cookie internally, with the real Host/Origin. No launch URL or token is
returned by this package. Native TLS decides Secure. HTTP responses append
Set-Cookie; upgrades can internally bootstrap admission without exposing
authentication URLs, with cookies persisted by the next HTTP request. Native
Connection owns all API/WS protocol and lifecycle behavior.

Exec readiness connects to /tmp/dsh-forward-auth-ready.sock and requires exactly
ready followed by newline. This UID-owned mode 0600 Unix socket has no public
route; it answers only while the gate is registered and the Host has a bound
port. Disposal removes the socket. There is no unauthenticated HTTP health
exception.

The exact-source manager patch adds this package to native protectedModules,
so row disable and bundle deselection/removal are management-required; direct
installation/update of protected module names is denied. Rootfs packaging must
pin host-webserver, client-connection, plugin-manager, app-boot and this package;
prevent writable profile dependencies from shadowing those modules. Independent
market managers require the same policy. These are required packaging controls,
not a sandbox against an owner who can execute arbitrary harness code.
Hot uninstall or dependency reload must dispose the gate before replacement;
with this package absent the patched Host denies all routes instead of exposing
the native launch-token route. Do not replace the patched Host at runtime.

Status logs
-----------
At startup the package logs one fixed line with the configured header, subject
count and trusted-proxy count, then state=waiting-for-edge. The first admitted
request logs state=active. Denials log state=waiting-for-edge or state=degraded
with a fixed reason and a rate limit; missing identity explicitly says the
edge/provider may not have injected a subject. Configuration, WebServer,
Connection, source and readiness contract failures log state=broken with a fixed
category and fail closed. No subject, header value, cookie, token or source
secret is logged.

Tavern corresponding source
--------------------------
When DSH_SOURCE_ARCHIVE=/opt/dsh/source/tavern.tar.gz and DSH_SOURCE_URL names
the public HTTPS revision of this distribution, startup validates the archive.
The exact GET/HEAD /distribution/source.tar.gz route streams that immutable
archive behind the same mandatory guard (other methods 405). tapIndex adds
visible Tavern AGPL source-download and distribution-revision links. No source
route or notice is registered when neither variable is configured. The archive
is provided by immutable packaging; persistent user data is never archived.
